# ========================================
# 🗑️ DELETE DEVICE - IP RELEASE VS DELETE FLAG
# ========================================

### 71. Create Device for Delete-IP Flag Test (default: release)
# @name createDeviceForReleaseTest
POST {{baseUrl}}/{{apiVersion}}/devices
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{deviceAuth.response.body.token}}

{
  "name": "device for release-ip delete test",
  "device_type_id": 1,
  "ip_addresses": [25]
}

### 72. Delete Device - Default Behavior (releases IP to 'reserved', does not delete it)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/{{apiVersion}}/devices/{{createDeviceForReleaseTest.response.body.data.id}}
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{deviceAuth.response.body.token}}

### 73. Verify Released IP Still Exists, Status = reserved
GET {{baseUrl}}/{{apiVersion}}/ip-addresses/25
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{deviceAuth.response.body.token}}

### 74. Create Device for Delete-IP Flag Test (explicit delete_ip=true)
# @name createDeviceForDeleteIpTest
POST {{baseUrl}}/{{apiVersion}}/devices
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{deviceAuth.response.body.token}}

{
  "name": "device for delete-ip=true delete test",
  "device_type_id": 1,
  "ip_addresses": [26]
}

### 75. Delete Device with delete_ip=true (permanently deletes its IP)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/{{apiVersion}}/devices/{{createDeviceForDeleteIpTest.response.body.data.id}}?delete_ip=true
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{deviceAuth.response.body.token}}

### 76. Verify Deleted IP No Longer Exists (Should 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/{{apiVersion}}/ip-addresses/26
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{deviceAuth.response.body.token}}

# ========================================
# ✅ DEVICES API TEST CHECKLIST
# ========================================
# 
# BASIC CRUD OPERATIONS:
# ⏳ GET /api/v1/devices (get all devices with filtering and pagination)
# ⏳ GET /api/v1/devices/:id (get device by ID with full details)
# ⏳ POST /api/v1/devices (create new device)
# ⏳ PUT /api/v1/devices/:id (update device)
# ⏳ DELETE /api/v1/devices/:id (delete device)
#
# SEARCH CAPABILITIES:
# ⏳ Search by device name
# ⏳ Search by manufacturer
# ⏳ Search by platform
# ⏳ Search by IP address
# ⏳ Search by description
# ⏳ Search with pagination
#
# FILTERING CAPABILITIES:
# ⏳ Filter by device_type_id (single and multiple)
# ⏳ Filter by platform_id (single and multiple)
# ⏳ Filter by location
# ⏳ Filter by tags (array of tag IDs)
# ⏳ Combined filters (all parameters together)
#
# PAGINATION:
# ⏳ Page number control (page parameter, default: 1)
# ⏳ Page size control (pageSize parameter, default: 10)
# ⏳ Pagination with filters
#
# FIELD VALIDATION:
# ⏳ No required fields (all optional)
# ⏳ Name validation: if provided, must not be empty (converted to lowercase)
# ⏳ Device type validation: if provided, must not be empty and must exist
# ⏳ IP addresses validation: if provided, must not be empty array and all IDs must exist
# ⏳ Platform validation: if provided, must exist
# ⏳ Tags validation: all IDs must exist
# ⏳ Contacts validation: all IDs must exist
# ⏳ Device name uniqueness validation (case-insensitive)
# ⏳ Partial update support (only provided fields updated)
#
# ERROR HANDLING:
# ⏳ 400 - Invalid data/empty required fields when provided
# ⏳ 400 - Invalid relationship IDs (device_type, platform, ip_addresses, tags, contacts)
# ⏳ 404 - Device not found
